# ── `*.regressions` — the SIMULATION runner's seed cache. NOT the proptest corpus. ──
# `simulation/src/runner.rs` appends a bare hex seed per failing simulation run
# (`append_regression_seed`) and REMOVES it again as soon as that seed passes
# (`remove_passing_regression_seed`). It is therefore a self-pruning working set, not a
# durable record: a seed that stops reproducing deletes itself. Nothing is lost by not
# tracking it. Written to `simulate_{lang}.regressions` at the workspace root by
# `macros/src/gen/test_gen/simulation_binary.rs:206`.
#
# ⚠ Its name is one token away from `*.proptest-regressions` below, and that similarity is
# part of how the proptest corpora stayed hidden for so long: a reader who has already
# accepted "regressions files are regenerable scratch" carries that belief onto a rule that
# governs a completely different artifact. The two rules are deliberately NOT merged, and
# the block below states why the opposite policy applies there.
*.regressions
prattail-parser-*.rs

# ── proptest counterexample corpora — TRACKED DELIBERATELY, both layouts ──
#
# A proptest corpus is a list of seeds for inputs that ONCE FALSIFIED A PROPERTY, with the
# shrunk counterexample recorded beside each. It is NOT regenerable on demand: reproducing
# one means re-running the random search that found it, which may take an unbounded number
# of cases or may never recur at all once the surrounding grammar drifts. proptest says so
# itself, in the header it writes into every one of these files verbatim:
#
#     "It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
#      everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases."
#
# Two DISTINCT on-disk layouts exist in this repository, and a rule for one does not cover
# the other. Both are un-ignored here, by name:
#
#   LAYOUT B — `<proptest_corpus_dir>/gen_<lang>_prop.proptest-regressions`
#     The pinned `FileFailurePersistence::Direct` form emitted by
#     `macros/src/gen/test_gen/mod.rs::proptest_config_expr`. `proptest_corpus_dir` is
#     declared in `[package.metadata.mettail]` (see `ast::manifest`); it is
#     `languages/tests` today. ⚠ The file name is keyed on the LANGUAGE NAME, not on the
#     test file — every generated property test of a language shares ONE corpus — so
#     renaming a language STRANDS its corpus silently.
#     `ast/tests/language_name_keyed_artifacts.rs::every_prop_corpus_names_a_live_language`
#     is the guard that makes that loud.
#
#   LAYOUT A — `<crate>/proptest-regressions/<module path>.txt`
#     proptest's DEFAULT `FileFailurePersistence::SourceParallel` form, derived from
#     `file!()`. Used by every hand-written `proptest!` block (macros/, prattail/,
#     rholang-runtime/, rigail/). ⚠ The path is keyed on the SOURCE FILE, so MOVING a
#     property strands its corpus just as silently — and by two routes the layout-B guard
#     cannot see: the properties moving crate (`prattail/src/automata/lex_weight.rs` ->
#     `rigail/src/lex_weight.rs`) and a flat module becoming a directory
#     (`prattail/src/decision_tree.rs` -> `prattail/src/decision_tree/tests.rs`).
#     `testkit/tests/proptest_corpus_replay_paths.rs` is the guard for this layout; it
#     inverts proptest's own `SourceParallel` resolution rather than consulting a list.
!*.proptest-regressions
!**/proptest-regressions/
!**/proptest-regressions/**

# Rustc internal compiler error reports (rustc panics; user-local)
